(archive-note
  :date        "2026-07-29"
  :archived-on "2026-08-02"
  :what        "73 `.retag-new` sidecar chapters — a complete, unpromoted schema migration of the reference."
  :provenance  "generated 2026-07-29; found untracked in scheme/reference/ on 2026-08-02 and archived here rather than promoted or deleted."
  :training-eligible #f
  :confidentiality public
  :status      "needs-alfred"
  :note
"The migration folds the three flat program keys — `:eng-program`, `:math-program`,
`:cs-program` — into one `:programs` list whose entries carry `:code` and `:tags`:

    :eng-program  \"(...)\"                         ->  :programs ((:code \"(...)\" :tags (eng program))
    :math-program \"(...)\"                                       (:code \"(...)\" :tags (math program))
    :cs-program   \"(...)\"                                       (:code \"(...)\" :tags (cs program)))

It is NOT promoted, and promoting it is a decision for Alfred, not a cleanup.
As of 2026-08-02 six live scripts read the flat keys and NOTHING reads
`:programs`:

    scripts/pre-fold-inspection.py
    scripts/fix-auto-generated-stubs.py
    scripts/test-in-session-libs.py
    scripts/compliance-check-runnable.py
    scripts/mark-failing-rows-spec-only.py
    scripts/cpt-prep/emit_cpt_v5.py

So landing these files as-is would silently empty the program slot for every
consumer — the reference would still parse and would still LOOK complete while
every runnable example vanished. That is the exact silent-wrong failure the
conformance work of 2026-08-02 was spent eliminating, so the files are parked
here intact until the six readers are migrated in the same pass.

Nothing in the live reference was changed by this archival. The 73 chapters
these shadow are untouched on their canonical paths.")
